== Origin of the logic ==

Spyhound is a Kotlin reimplementation of the detection logic of the
Zero Breach Toolkit (Apache License 2.0):
https://github.com/interplains/Zero-Breach-Toolkit

== Indicator sources ==

The indicators are listed in app/src/main/assets/iocs/sources.json. Each
source is pinned to a fixed commit and verified by SHA-256 before use.

Bundled with the app:

1. MVT project, mvt-indicators (MIT License)
   https://github.com/mvt-project/mvt-indicators
   Indicators credited to: Meta, Amnesty International, Citizen Lab, Cisco,
   Inside Story, iVerify (Intellexa Predator); Google, Lookout (RCS Lab);
   Citizen Lab, Microsoft (QuaDream KingSpawn); Kaspersky Lab (Operation
   Triangulation); Lookout (WyrmSpy and DragonEgg; EagleMsgSpy); Microsoft,
   Recorded Future (Candiru); Reporters Without Borders, RESIDENT.NGO
   (ResidentBat); Citizen Lab (Cellebrite); Google Threat Intelligence
   Group, iVerify, Lookout (DarkSword); Google Threat Intelligence Group,
   iVerify (Coruna); Osservatorio Nessuno (Morpheus, Spyrtacus); ESET,
   Cyble Research, Zimperium (BTMOB).

2. ECHAP stalkerware-indicators (Creative Commons Attribution 4.0)
   https://github.com/AssoEchap/stalkerware-indicators
   Cite: ECHAP
   License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

3. Zero Breach Toolkit, curated lists (CC0 1.0)
   https://github.com/interplains/Zero-Breach-Toolkit

Not bundled, loaded onto the device only when the user updates indicators:

4. Amnesty International, AmnestyTech/investigations
   https://github.com/AmnestyTech/investigations
   Cites: Amnesty International (2021); Amnesty International, Google
   (Android campaign 2023); Amnesty International (Wintego Helios, 2024;
   NoviSpy, 2024); Amnesty International (2018-08-01), NSO Group
   infrastructure; Amnesty International (2019-10-10), Morocco; Meta,
   Citizen Lab, Amnesty International (2021-12-16); Amnesty International
   (2020-09-25), FinSpy for Windows, Android and Linux.

5. The Citizen Lab, citizenlab/malware-indicators
   https://github.com/citizenlab/malware-indicators
   Cites: The Citizen Lab, 'The Million Dollar Dissident' (2016-08);
   'Champing at the Cyberbit' (2017-12); 'The Kingdom Came to Canada'
   (2018-10); 'Reckless Exploit' (2017-06), Mexico; 'Reckless Redux'
   (2017-06), Mexico; 'Insider Information' (2017-07), Mexico.

These two repositories carry no license that permits redistribution, so
Spyhound does not ship their data. The app downloads it directly from the
original repositories at the pinned commits.
